The files in this directory consist of metadata files, reduced Keck LRIS data,
coadded LRIS data, and files related to the reduction of LRIS data.
The metadata files are in IPAC format and link the reduced data and its
related files to the original KOAIDs they were reduced from.

Data reduction and coaddition was performed in an automated way, and a
semi-automated vetting process was used as well. However, these data should
not be used for science without further vetting. The information needed
to check the quality of the data is here provided.


Directory Hierarchy
===================
The files have been grouped by the target that was observed, the UT date of
the observation, and the LRIS arm the data came from, as follows:

${target}/${UT date}/${instrument}

For example:

J1030+0524/20120415/LRIS/

The instrument component is either "LRIS" for the red arm or "LRISBLUE" for the
blue arm. The two arms are reduced separately, so a night on which both arms
were used appears as two directories.

These are the subdirectories under this hierarchy containing the reduced data:

- ${spectrograph}_A/: The results of a PypeIt reduction of the raw data. The
                      spectrograph name is the one PypeIt reduced the data
                      with, and depends on the arm and on the date of the
                      observation, because the LRIS detectors were upgraded
                      several times. It is one of keck_lris_red_orig,
                      keck_lris_red, keck_lris_red_mark4, keck_lris_blue_orig
                      or keck_lris_blue. The "_A" suffix is PypeIt's name for
                      the instrument configuration that was reduced.
- 1D_Coadd/:          The results of flux calibrating and coadding the 1D
                      reduced spectra. Because a coadd combines more than one
                      of the directories above, it is stored higher in the
                      hierarchy than the reductions that went into it.

Within a ${spectrograph}_A directory:

- Science/:      The spec1d and spec2d files produced from the science frames.
- Calibrations/: The calibration frames PypeIt built from the arcs and flats.

2D coaddition was not performed for these data.

File Formats
============

spec1d files
------------
FITS files beginning with the prefix 'spec1d' contain calibrated 1d spectra
extracted from the science data during the main data reduction. See
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/out_spec1D.html
for a detailed description of these files.

spec1d text files
-----------------
Text files beginning with the prefix 'spec1d' contain extraction information
about each spec1d FITS file. More information about these files can be found at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/out_spec1D.html#extraction-information.

spec2d
------
FITS files with the 'spec2d' prefix contain a 2D spectral image created by
PypeIt during the data reduction. They are described in detail at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/out_spec2D.html.

calibration files
-----------------
The FITS files in the Calibrations subdirectory are the processed calibration
frames (arcs, flats, wavelength solutions, slit edge traces and the like)
that PypeIt built from the raw calibrations and applied to the science frames.
They are described at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/calibrations.html.

1D coadd output files
---------------------
FITS files that begin with the prefix 'coadd1d' are coadded 1D spectra from
multiple exposures of a single object. They are described in detail at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/coadd1d.html#current-coadd1d-data-model.
When available, the optimally extracted (Horne 1986) spectra are used for the
coaddition, otherwise the boxcar extracted spectra are used. This information
is contained in the coadded 1D file header, along with a HISTORY block naming
every spec1d file and extracted object that went into the coadd.
Before coadding, a relative flux calibration is applied to the 1D spectra using
a sensitivity function derived from standard stars observed in the same
instrument configuration (see
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/fluxing.html). The sensitivity
functions themselves are not included in this archive.
NOTE: A spectrum with relative flux calibration is expressed in units of
[1e-17 erg/s/cm^2/Ang], have the correct shape over the wavelength range and
differ from an absolute calibration only in the normalization.

pypeit files
------------
Files ending in ".pypeit" are the original PypeIt reduction files that were
used to guide the reduction of the raw data.  These are text files and are
described at https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/pypeit_file.html.
Frames that were deliberately left out of the reduction appear in these files
commented out, so the full set of frames the reduction started from can still
be read off.

calibration association files
-----------------------------
Files ending in ".calib" record which raw frames were combined into each
processed calibration, and which science frames those calibrations were applied
to. More information about these files can be found at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/calibrations.html.

parameter files
---------------
Files ending in ".par" contain the original PypeIt parameters used for 
processing the files, in a "ini" format. More information about these
parameters can be found at 
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/pypeit_par.html.

QA files
--------
Each reduction directory contains a "QA.tar.gz" archive holding the quality
assessment plots PypeIt generated for that reduction. These are described at
https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/qa.html.

log files
---------
log files containing information about the reduction and the 1D coadding
processes are available in each subdirectory.

Metadata Files
==============

reduced_files_meta.dat
----------------------

The reduced_files_meta.dat file contains metadata for the spec1d and spec2d files.
This file is organized by KOAID of the original raw data. Below is the description
of the columns in this file. All filenames are relative to the top level of
this directory.

+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| Column Name   | Description                                                 |
+===============+=============================================================+
| koaid         | The KOAID of the raw image that was reduced.                |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| spec1d_file   | The filename of the spec1d file.                            |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| spec1d_info   | The filename of the extraction info text file associated    |
|               | with a spec1d file.                                         |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| spec2d_file   | The filename of the spec2d file.                            |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| pypeit_file   | The PypeIt reduction file used to reduce the data.          |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| ra            | Target right ascension (deg) from the raw image header.     |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| dec           | Target declination (deg) from the raw image header.         |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| target        | TARGET name from the raw image header.                      |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| progpi        | Program Principle Investigator from the raw image header.   |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| semester      | Observing schedule semester from the raw image header.      |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| progid        | Program ID from the raw image header.                       |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| dispname      | The grating (red arm) or grism (blue arm) used for the raw  |
|               | image.                                                      |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| slmsknam      | The DECKER value from the raw image header, which for LRIS  |
|               | names the longslit or slit mask that was in place.          |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| binning       | Binning from the raw image header.                          |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| mjd           | Modified Julian Date from the raw image header.             |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| airmass       | Airmass from the raw image header.                          |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| exptime       | Exposure time from the raw image header.                    |
+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+

coadded_files_meta.dat
----------------------
A coadded_files_meta.dat file is written alongside reduced_files_meta.dat, but
it is not populated in this release: the per-object metadata it is built from
was produced by a collation step that is not part of the LRIS reduction. The
provenance of each coadded spectrum, the spec1d files and the individual
extracted objects that were combined to make it, is instead recorded in the
HISTORY keywords of the coadd1d FITS file itself, and each of those spec1d
files has a row in reduced_files_meta.dat.

Software Used
-------------
All data was reduced with PypeIt (https://pypeit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/).
Additional software used to generate this archive and run the PypeIt software is
located at https://github.com/pypeit/adap.
